# Browser
# What the page shows of a Case (CR 719.3): unsolved, its "Solved" line is greyed, since the ability may affect the game only
# once the Case is solved (CR 719.3c), and nothing is written at its foot; once its "To solve" ability has made it solved, the
# card says SOLVED and the "To solve" line, which can do nothing more (CR 719.3a), is the greyed one. Bot1 casts the Case on
# turn 1 with four cards in hand at the end step (unsolved), and on turn 3 casts every Ornithopter it holds: solved.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Case of the Crimson Pulse
Ornithopter x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Case of the Crimson Pulse.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Ornithopter)
[T2 Bot2.Upkeep]
? Client.Bot1.Battlefield.Case of the Crimson Pulse.Status =
? Client.Bot1.Battlefield.Case of the Crimson Pulse.Rules = When this Case enters, discard a card, then draw two cards. / To solve — You have no cards in hand. (If unsolved, solve at the beginning of your end step.) / (grey) Solved — At the beginning of your upkeep, discard your hand, then draw two cards.
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T4 Bot2.Upkeep]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Case of the Crimson Pulse.Solved = true
? Client.Bot1.Battlefield.Case of the Crimson Pulse.Status = SOLVED
? Client.Bot1.Battlefield.Case of the Crimson Pulse.Rules = When this Case enters, discard a card, then draw two cards. / (grey) To solve — You have no cards in hand. (If unsolved, solve at the beginning of your end step.) / Solved — At the beginning of your upkeep, discard your hand, then draw two cards.

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Case of the Crimson Pulse.Solved = true
Bot1.Hand.Count = 0
Bot1.Graveyard = Ornithopter
